> Isolate one noiseless Gaussian Langevin step

For Gaussian mean(.3,-.2) and variance(.49,.25), the force at(.79,.05) is(1,1). With alpha.02 and zero innovation the ULA update subtracts.01 from both coordinates. The report supplies the innovation and differentiates the actual energy.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/energy_langevin_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");auto x=n::from_vector(std::vector<float>{.79f,.05f},{1,2}).requires_grad_();auto path=m::ConfiningEnergy(nullptr,x,true);auto force=n::grad(n::sum(path.energy),{x})[0];auto next=x-.01*force;auto values=n::concat({force.reshape({2}),next.reshape({2})},0);if(n::max(n::abs(force-1.)).item()>2e-7)return 1;
std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");auto v=values.to_vector<double>();for(size_t i=0;i<v.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,v[i]);n::save_npz("build/energy_langevin_worked.npz",{{"values",values}});dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(n::arange(0,std::int64_t(v.size())).to_vector<double>(),v,"native values",{37,99,235}).title("Isolate one noiseless Gaussian Langevin step").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/energy_langevin_worked.svg");}
```
